remstart
    THE DIVER
    the diver from the boat can come down to the board, with a camera. the routines are in
    fish_routines_diver, and the tests are in fish_tests_diver.

    HOW THE DIVER COMES DOWN. a bottle wants to sink: on the bottom row it pays out. a bottle that a
    swap carries up to the top row, from the row under it, does the other thing. it is gone, and the
    diver is in its cell. a bottle that was left on the top row by a group that popped there does not
    count, and neither does one that is swapped along the top row. stepLiveMove, in fish_funcs, asks
    diverBottleRose after every swap.

    WHAT THE DIVER IS. it is a kind of fish of its own, the one after the kinds of the quests, so it
    is a fish like any other to the board: it can be swapped, it falls, and it is saved with the board.
    it never matches, because no kind from QUEST_SOLID_FROM up does. and nothing happens to it: it is
    never stung, never belly up, never stacked, never copied, and a stingray swims past it. there is
    only ever one. diverMend, which handle_combos calls before every look at the board, sees to all
    of that, whatever a special move may have done.

    THE PICTURES. whenever a fish pops in one of the four cells that touch the diver, for whatever
    reason, the diver takes its picture. a fish that is belly up, or a skeleton, is not worth one.
    there is no flash, because nobody uses one down here. the diver turns to the fish and holds its
    camera out, and the corners of a viewfinder close in on the fish. the fish do not pop until that
    is done: every pop of that look at the board is held back for DIVER_SNAP_AHEAD. then they pop, and
    a little photo paper flies from the fish to its box of the album. a fish that the album has
    already gets none of that: the diver does not look up, and nothing waits. diverSnapAhead is what holds the pops back. it has to
    say so before handle_combos has gone through the groups, so it goes by which groups are big
    enough. a fish that only pops because a stingray shot past it is not held back for.
    there is a picture to take of each of the seven fish, of the jellyfish and of the stingray: nine.
    the pictures that have been taken are kept for the whole game, from one dive to the next, and they
    are saved with it. diverJudge takes them, when handle_combos has decided what pops.

    THE AIR. the diver has DIVER_AIR_MAX moves of air. every move that is counted takes one, whether
    it moved the diver or not. when the air is gone and the board has settled, the diver swims up to
    the top row, trading places with the fish over it, one row after another, and then up and away,
    and a fish takes its place. the game waits while it does. diver_rise does that. another bottle
    brings the diver back, with a full tank.

    THE ALBUM. nine pale blue boxes in a row, under the bars of the coral, one for every picture. a box
    has its fish in it once the picture has been taken. they show from the first dive of a game on.
    the air sits on top of them while the diver is down: a row of little blocks, one for every move of
    air that a full tank has. the ones that are left are bright, and the ones that are used up are dim.

    HOW THE DIVER IS DRAWN. the picture of its kind, Diver.png, is empty, so its cell on the board
    looks empty. the diver is one sprite of its own, on top of that cell, which goes wherever the
    sprite of the cell goes. its frames are in DiverSheet.png: swimming, swimming with the camera held
    out, and upright, which is how it goes up. the art is the pixel art diver of dkproductions, and
    the frames with the camera were added to it. make_diver.py, which is not part of the game, built the sheet.

    WHEN THE LAST PICTURE IS TAKEN the diver is done, and goes up as soon as the board has settled.
    DIVER_DONE is 1 from then on, and no bottle brings the diver back. that is the end of the game.
    see THE ENDING, further down.
remend

global TEX_DIVER `the kind of fish that the diver is. load_textures, in fish_routines, loads its picture right after the kinds of the quests.

global DIVER_AIR_MAX = 8 `how many moves of air a dive has
global DIVER_AIR_LOW = 3 `the bar of air blinks from here down

global DIVER_ON = 0 `1 while the diver is on the board
global DIVER_AT = -1 `the cell that it was in, the last time that the board was looked at
global DIVER_AIR = 0 `how many moves of air are left
global DIVER_SEEN = 0 `1 once the diver has come down in this game. the album shows from then on.
global DIVER_DONE = 0 `1 once every picture has been taken

global DIVER_ALBUM_COUNT = 9
global dim DIVER_ALBUM_KIND(9) `the kind of fish that every box of the album is for
global dim DIVER_PHOTOS(9) `1 for every picture that has been taken
global dim DIVER_PHOTO_MS(9) `when each one shows up in its box. the fish has to pop first.

` how the album is drawn. the boxes are in one row. a fish in a box is half of its size, so that the
` row is not much wider than the bars of the coral are.
global DIVER_BOX_SIZE = 8
global DIVER_BOX_STEP = 9
global DIVER_FISH_SIZE = 8 `how big the fish in a box is
global DIVER_LEAVE_TIME = 900 `how long the diver takes to swim up and away, in milliseconds

global dim DIVER_BOX_SPRITES(9)
global dim DIVER_FISH_SPRITES(9)
global DIVER_AIR_PIP_ROOM = 16 `the most blocks of air that there is room to draw. DIVER_AIR_MAX can be no more than this.
global dim DIVER_AIR_PIPS(16)

` the diver itself. see HOW THE DIVER IS DRAWN.
global TEX_DIVER_SHEET
global TEX_DIVER_FOCUS `the corners of a viewfinder
global TEX_DIVER_PHOTO `a little photo paper
global DIVER_FRAMES = 12 `how many frames every row of the sheet has
global DIVER_FRAME_MS = 90 `how long a frame lasts
global DIVER_BODY_SPRITE = 0
global DIVER_LEAVE_SPRITE = 0
global DIVER_LEAVE_MS = -100000 `when the diver started up
global DIVER_LEAVE_X = 0
global DIVER_LEAVE_Y = 0

` THE SHOTS. a shot is one fish that the diver is taking a picture of. there is room for four at once,
` which is every cell that touches the diver.
global DIVER_SHOT_COUNT = 4
global DIVER_FOCUS_TIME = 380 `how long before the fish pops the viewfinder starts to close in on it, in milliseconds
global DIVER_FOCUS_HOLD = 140 `and how long after the pop it stays
global DIVER_PAPER_TIME = 520 `how long the photo paper takes to fly to its box
global DIVER_SHOT_NEXT = 0 `the one that the next shot takes
global dim DIVER_SHOT_ON(4)
global dim DIVER_SHOT_MS(4) `when the fish pops
global dim DIVER_SHOT_SLOT(4) `the box that the paper flies to
global dim DIVER_SHOT_X(4) `where the fish is
global dim DIVER_SHOT_Y(4)
global dim DIVER_FOCUS_SPRITES(4)
global dim DIVER_PAPER_SPRITES(4)
global dim DIVER_PAPER_FISH(4) `the fish on the paper
global DIVER_SNAP_AHEAD = 430 `how long the pops are held back for the diver to take its pictures, in milliseconds
global DIVER_SNAP_HOLD = 0 `how long the pops of this look at the board are being held back for it. diverSnapAhead works it out.
global DIVER_FACE_LEFT = 0 `1 while the diver faces left. it turns to the way that it was moved, and to the fish that it takes a picture of.
global DIVER_LAST_COLUMN = -1 `the column that it was drawn in on the frame before, or -1
global DIVER_RISE_DUE = 0 `1 when the diver is to swim up and away, and has not started
global DIVER_RISE_HAPPY = 0 `1 when it goes with every picture taken
global DIVER_RISING = 0 `1 while it is swimming up
global DIVER_RISE_FRAMES = 27 `how many frames it takes to get up one row. it is slow, so that it can be seen for what it is.
global DIVER_RISE_WAIT_FRAMES = 24 `and how many frames it waits, upright, before it sets off
global DIVER_SNAPS = 0 `how many pictures the last look at the board took. the tests read this.

` THE SOUNDS. there is a splash when the diver comes down. and while it is down, there is the sound of
` being under the water with it, which is a recording that loops, turned well down so that it sits
` under everything else. it fades in after the splash, and out again when the diver goes up.
global SFX_CLIP_DIVER_SPLASH
global SFX_CLIP_DIVER_WATER
global SFX_DIVER_SPLASH = 0
global SFX_DIVER_WATER = 0
global DIVER_SPLASH_VOLUME# = .6 `how loud the splash is, from 0 to 1
global DIVER_WATER_VOLUME# = .22 `how loud the recording gets
global DIVER_WATER_NOW# = 0 `how loud it is on this frame. it chases what it should be.
global DIVER_WATER_STARTED = 0 `1 once it has been played. it is turned down after that, and never stopped.

remstart
    THE ENDING. when the last picture has been taken, and the board has settled, the game is over, the
    same way that it is over when the reef is saved or the ancient one is summoned: this is a third
    ending of the hidden game. handle_coral_ending, in fish_routines_coral, starts it.
      - on the board, the words say that the album is full, and hearts come up from the fish. diver_finale.
      - the initials and the table of high scores come up, as they do for every game that ends.
      - the wave that brings the main menu back is photo papers of the fish, in place of bubbles.
        diverWaveStart, diverWaveStep and diverWaveEnd, which menu_transition and frame_transition call.
      - at the surface, before the menu is there, the photos are strung on a line along the side of
        the boat, under its railing. the diver on the back of the boat is hunched over, looking
        through the rest of them, which are not seen. a heart comes up from it now and then. and the
        words are there. diver_boat_scene, which handle_game_end comes to.
    and the main menu remembers: the photos are on the boat from then on, and the diver is hunched
    over them, with a heart once in a while. diverSurfaceStep, which frame_surface calls, draws it.
    the player can turn that off again on the options page, with "Menu photos", which is only on the
    page once there are photos to turn off. the FISH_MENU_DIVER environment variable puts them
    there, for working on the game.
    a game that ended this way has a diving mask for its badge in the table of high scores.
    the pictures of the boat with the diver hunched over, and the badge, are built by
    make_diver_menu_art.py, which is not part of the game.

    THE CODEC has an entry for the diver, which says what info mode says about it, and is unlocked
    the first time that the diver comes down. and it has one for this ending, which is locked, and
    says nothing about what it is, until a game has ended this way. see setup_codec, in fish_routines_codec.
remend
#constant CORAL_ENDING_DIVER 3
#constant PREF_ENDING_DIVER 12
global DIVER_ENDING_DUE = 0 `1 when the album is full, and the ending has not started yet
global DIVER_ENDING_HOLD = 0 `1 keeps the ending from starting. the tests set it, because the ending draws frames of its own.
global DIVER_SURFACE = 0 `1 once some game has ended with the album full
global DIVER_SURFACE_READY = 0 `1 once the things that are drawn into the main menu have been put there
global DIVER_SCENE = 0 `1 while the scene at the boat is playing
global DIVER_SCENE_MS = 0 `when it started
global DIVER_SCENE_KEEP# = 1 `how much of the words is there, from 0 to 1. they fade out at the end.
global DIVER_SCENE_HOLD_MS = 3200 `how long it is before the player can move on
global DIVER_SCENE_MAX_MS = 18000 `and how long before it moves on by itself
global DIVER_HEART_MS = 0 `when the next heart comes up from the diver on the boat

` the wave of photo papers
global DIVER_WAVE_COUNT = 22 `there is room for 30
global DIVER_WAVE_ON = 0
global dim DIVER_WAVE_SPRITES(30)
global dim DIVER_WAVE_FISH(30)
global dim DIVER_WAVE_X(30)
global dim DIVER_WAVE_OFF(30) `how far ahead of the waterline each one is, or behind it
global dim DIVER_WAVE_PHASE(30)

` the line of photos on the boat. everything is measured from the middle of the picture of the boat.
global DIVER_LINE_LEFT = -60 `where the two ends of the line are, across
global DIVER_LINE_RIGHT = 50
global DIVER_LINE_DOWN = 16 `how far down they are, which is just under the railing, at the top of the hull
global DIVER_LINE_SAG = 2 `how far the middle of the line hangs under its ends
global DIVER_LINE_DOT_COUNT = 40
global dim DIVER_LINE_DOTS(40)
global dim DIVER_LINE_PAPERS(9)
global dim DIVER_LINE_FISH(9)
global DIVER_HEART_X = 61 `where the hearts come up from, which is the head of the diver on the boat
global DIVER_HEART_Y = -4
global TEX_DIVER_BOAT `the picture of the boat with the diver hunched over
global DIVER_BOAT_SWAPPED = 0 `1 while the boat of the main menu is that picture
#constant PREF_MENU_PHOTOS 13
global OPTION_MENU_PHOTOS = 1 `1 while the photos are wanted on the main menu
global TEX_BADGE_MASK `the badge of a game that ended with the album full, in the table of high scores

` the two entries of the codec. setup_codec, in fish_routines_codec, says which they are.
global CODEC_ENTRY_DIVER = -1
global CODEC_ENTRY_ALBUM = -1 `the ending
global TEX_CODEC_DIVER `the pictures that they have there
global TEX_ENDING_ALBUM

` info mode has a spot for the album, once the diver has come down in a game
global INFO_INDEX_DIVER = -1
global DIVER_INFO_TOP = -1 `where that spot was put last. it follows the album.
global DIVER_CARD_TEXT_ID = 0
global DIVER_CARD_SUB_TEXT_ID = 0
